WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.544 --> 00:00:04.711
- My personal style in three
words is goofy, teacher, boy.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.473
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:17.383
- I think my personal style is dapper,

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.880
it's sexy, it's functional.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.818
I really want people to see
that I'm like a creative,

00:00:22.818 --> 00:00:25.418
I'm a dreamer, I'm like a powerful woman,

00:00:25.418 --> 00:00:28.386
you know, someone who is out
here and just killing it.

00:00:28.386 --> 00:00:30.180
- I like to combine both masculine

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.383
and feminine energies in the way I dress.

00:00:32.383 --> 00:00:34.498
Anyone can buy fashion,
anyone can learn fashion

00:00:34.498 --> 00:00:37.596
down at the school, but style
is something that is internal

00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:39.227
that you carry with you throughout life.

00:00:39.227 --> 00:00:40.976
I'm all about my style, baby.

00:00:40.976 --> 00:00:44.202
- I've always dressed on the
more masculine side of things.

00:00:44.202 --> 00:00:47.170
It was cargo shorts in
middle school and then again

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:50.017
in college and now thank God
the cargo shorts are gone.

00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:52.503
- My clothes make me feel confident,

00:00:52.503 --> 00:00:53.929
they make me feel like myself.

00:00:53.929 --> 00:00:55.276
They make me feel joyful.

00:00:55.276 --> 00:00:56.746
- I feel like gender is fluidity

00:00:56.746 --> 00:00:59.059
as has been said a million
times over and over again,

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:02.436
but it's truth, and my gender is fluidity.

00:01:02.436 --> 00:01:04.602
Being a bigger body, it's
harder to find things

00:01:04.602 --> 00:01:06.030
that feel like they have the right fit

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:09.166
and feel like they're
the right style for me.

00:01:09.166 --> 00:01:12.475
- When I was growing up, I wore
a lot of dresses and heels,

00:01:12.475 --> 00:01:13.795
and I looked very nice in them,

00:01:13.795 --> 00:01:16.311
but it just wasn't what
I was comfortable in.

00:01:16.311 --> 00:01:17.861
- Sometimes I might have something long

00:01:17.861 --> 00:01:20.092
and very extremely feminine, but sometimes

00:01:20.092 --> 00:01:22.535
I'll do a dungaree or a jumper

00:01:22.535 --> 00:01:24.012
and a baseball cap to the back.

00:01:24.012 --> 00:01:25.182
It really depends on my mood.

00:01:25.182 --> 00:01:28.073
- I want my clothes to make me feel

00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:31.327
like the sort of goofy,
butchy mask that I am.

00:01:31.327 --> 00:01:33.851
- I don't shop at stores too often.

00:01:33.851 --> 00:01:36.213
It's very difficult to
find anything there for me,

00:01:36.213 --> 00:01:39.350
but I hope that anyone who
looks at me is inspired

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.700
to do whatever they want
to do to express themselves

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.015
and not ask for anyone's permission.

00:01:45.015 --> 00:01:47.417
- I would have to say Jaden
Smith is the fashion icon.

00:01:47.417 --> 00:01:49.086
Dresses and flower crowns.

00:01:49.086 --> 00:01:51.247
Boys in dresses, boys in dresses.

00:01:51.247 --> 00:01:52.184
- Who-Ha.

00:01:52.184 --> 00:01:54.952
(laughing)

00:01:54.952 --> 00:01:57.677
- I think non-binary
fashion to me is freedom.

00:01:57.677 --> 00:01:59.061
I would love to walk into a store

00:01:59.061 --> 00:02:01.668
and it's not based on men's
section, women's section,

00:02:01.668 --> 00:02:03.703
but really about the styles and the fits

00:02:03.703 --> 00:02:05.696
and the different body types.

00:02:05.696 --> 00:02:09.155
- No bounds, no walls, there's
no rules, there's no limits.

00:02:09.155 --> 00:02:13.322
Being an androgynous
person, like I don't care.

00:02:13.322 --> 00:02:14.831
If I like it, I'm gonna wear it.

00:02:14.831 --> 00:02:16.621
I'm gonna match it and style it

00:02:16.621 --> 00:02:19.266
so it fits my body and my lifestyle.

00:02:19.266 --> 00:02:22.281
- I think non-binary
fashion is just like a game

00:02:22.281 --> 00:02:25.084
of figuring out how I feel in a moment.

00:02:25.084 --> 00:02:27.389
- It allows us to dress ourselves

00:02:27.389 --> 00:02:30.119
the way we see ourselves within
and the way we feel within.

00:02:30.119 --> 00:02:32.926
- You know, clothing is based
off of societal constructs

00:02:32.926 --> 00:02:35.166
and so my expression of
that doesn't have to be

00:02:35.166 --> 00:02:37.809
what other people want me to look like.

00:02:37.809 --> 00:02:40.572
- Masculinity is just so fragile

00:02:40.572 --> 00:02:45.155
that any kind of change
towards it is just a oh my God.

00:02:45.155 --> 00:02:46.567
- I think it's really brave for people

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:50.559
to make the choice on a daily
or a weekly or a monthly basis

00:02:50.559 --> 00:02:53.801
to dress in a way that fits
their authentic selves.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.384
(upbeat music)

00:02:59.756 --> 00:03:01.260
We can see queerly here

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.483
(laughing)

00:03:02.483 --> 00:03:05.733
that gender is a complicated construct.

